<title>Lesson Activities</title>
<para>Here are the instructional activities for the lesson:</para>
<list>
  <item> 6.5.1: Undoing FOIL </item>
  <item> 6.5.2: Factoring Trinomials with Leading Coefficients of 1</item>
  <list>
    <item> 6.5.2: Self Check </item>
    <item> 6.5.2: Additional Resources </item>
  </list>
  <item> 6.5.3: Factoring Trinomials Using Trial and Error </item>
  <list>
    <item> 6.5.3: Self Check </item>
    <item> 6.5.3: Additional Resources </item>
  </list>
  <item> 6.5.4: Factoring Trinomials Using the “\(ac\)” Method and Substitution </item>
  <list>
    <item> 6.5.4: Self Check </item>
    <item> 6.5.4: Additional Resources </item>
  </list>
  <item> 6.5.5: Choosing Your Own Method to Factor Trinomials </item>
</list>
<para>Students will also complete a series of problems in the 6.5.6: Practice.</para>
<title>Required Materials</title>
<list>
  <item>Paper and pencil </item>
</list>
<title> Required Preparation</title>
<list>
  <item>None </item>
</list>
<title>Lesson Vocabulary</title>
<para>During this lesson, it is important to:</para>
<list>
  <item> Familiarize students with the vocabulary words they will see throughout the lesson. Encourage students to look
    for these words and notice their use and meanings. </item>
  <item> Encourage students to use key vocabulary words in “math talk” and their written and oral
    explanations. </item>
  <item> Utilize a word wall. Sample cards are located here: <link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/8ed3aa68763498713b44d3c2e537ffe61b4755f0">Mathematics Vocabulary Word Wall Cards</link> </item>
</list>
<para>Vocabulary words that are emphasized in this lesson include:</para>
